This mudlib includes objects that support a form of intermud communication.
The daemon support is in the /adm/daemon/inet directory.  Commands that
make use of this support include 'tell', 'finger', and 'mail'.  From inside
the mudlib, type 'finger @genocide' or 'finger @portals'.  Pick a likely
name from the list and type 'tell somebody@portals You stuf!, you.' or
try 'mail somebody@genocide'.

Use the 'where commandname' command in order to find where mail, tell,
finger, etc are in the mudlib.

The intermud code was originally written by Huthar@Portals.  It was later
updated by Blackthorn@Genocide so that it would work with Cynosure's
modifications to the socket efunctions (which were originally written
by Jacques [Dwayne Fontenot].  The intermud code is included mainly as an
example of how socket efunctions may be used.
